    "title": "Mixed results for tax levies in Ross County Election: Schools and seniors fall short, township renewals succeed - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By The Guardian ,\n1 days ago CHILLICOTHE, Ohio – Voters in Ross County delivered a split verdict on tax measures during Tuesday’s general election, rejecting proposed increases for education and senior services while approving renewals for local township operations. With 65 of 65 precincts reporting in unofficial tallies from the Ross County Board of Elections, the outcomes reflect community priorities amid ongoing debates over funding public services. Overall voter turnout was 33.52%, with absentee ballots playing a significant role in the levy races. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
